    },
    {
      "id": "RHuS5sKNSVv91xZpwiUtm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12066.265589114042,
      "y": 9483.435057661227,
      "width": 1617.9510498046875,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1676986008,
      "version": 224,
      "versionNonce": 116373480,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783866001619,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- This doesn't actually prevent concurrent inserts.\n- As no of bids per auction grows, you're locking more and more rows for each new bid. This creates a bottleneck with\n  increasing latency and poor user experience.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- This doesn't actually prevent concurrent inserts.\n- As no of bids per auction grows, you're locking more and more rows for each new bid. This creates a bottleneck with\n  increasing latency and poor user experience.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rqalhcx9wAZmKTIGb7KVw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12066.384476405086,
      "y": 9608.355878725391,
      "width": 1446.7591552734375,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1054832872,
      "version": 9,
      "versionNonce": 1723498472,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783866044204,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- You want to use row locking sparingly and with optimizations to ensure that \n a) you lock as few rows as possible and \n b) you lock rows for as short of a duration as possible. We don't respect either of these principles here.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- You want to use row locking sparingly and with optimizations to ensure that \n a) you lock as few rows as possible and \n b) you lock rows for as short of a duration as possible. We don't respect either of these principles here.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "PjMGPP971wcZmxb_N-SPt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12063.580717791316,
      "y": 9784.35860584132,
      "width": 1232.0274658203125,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 568100584,
      "version": 346,
      "versionNonce": 1400080616,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783866256843,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Good Solution: Cache maxBid externally\n- Cache maxBid for auction in Redis\n- Read maxBid for given auction from Redis\n- If neew bid higher, update cache with new maxBid\n- Write the bid to db with status of accepted\n\nChallenge:\nThere's no clean way to make Redis and a relational database transactionally consistent. \n Redis doesn't support distributed transaction protocols like two-phase commit",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Good Solution: Cache maxBid externally\n- Cache maxBid for auction in Redis\n- Read maxBid for given auction from Redis\n- If neew bid higher, update cache with new maxBid\n- Write the bid to db with status of accepted\n\nChallenge:\nThere's no clean way to make Redis and a relational database transactionally consistent. \n Redis doesn't support distributed transaction protocols like two-phase commit",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
